# Tsrust backend

The public greeting HTTP API listens on loopback port 4318.
Run tsrust dev, tsrust check and tsrust test.
Source is in app/api and app/lib; tests are in app/tests.
The api settings in tsrust.config.json select checked public operations and the
application-owned authorization policy. api:server supplies their compiler-owned
HTTP dispatch, description and OpenAPI handlers in memory. No generated server or
client directory is needed to build, check or start this service.

Start the service, then generate an independent client wherever you need it:

    tsrust api generate --url http://127.0.0.1:4318/api/description --out js-client
    tsrust api generate --url http://127.0.0.1:4318/api/description --language rust --out rust-client

A saved description works with --description api.json instead of --url.
Retain previous checked manifests or compatibility histories in app/ and list their
relative paths in api.compatible when deploying compatible API revisions. Bump the
API package version for releases and the API major for intentionally breaking wire
changes. SDK generation never changes the service's operations or dispatch.

Bring your own UI. No frontend toolchain or dependency installation is required.
Read AGENTS.md and app/api/access.tsr before exposing sensitive operations.
